# Git Remote Hygiene

## Canonical Remote

This repo has **one** remote: `origin` → `git@github.com:xiu-shi/maya_v1.0.git`

- Always push with: `git push origin main` (or `git push -u origin HEAD` on a feature branch)
- Never add a second remote pointing at the same GitHub URL under a different name
- `main` tracks `origin/main` only

## Before Reporting Push Failure

A push can succeed while `git status` still shows "ahead" if the upstream tracking ref is stale. **Never tell the user a push failed based on `git status` alone.**

After every push, verify sync with ALL of:

```bash
git fetch origin
git rev-parse HEAD origin/main   # SHAs must match
git status -sb                   # must NOT show "ahead"
```

If SHAs match but status still shows ahead, run:

```bash
git branch -u origin/main main
git fetch origin
```

Optionally confirm on GitHub:

```bash
gh api repos/xiu-shi/maya_v1.0/commits/main --jq '.sha[0:7]'
```

## After Push Checklist (Agent)

1. Run `git push origin main` (or current branch)
2. Run `git fetch origin`
3. Confirm `git rev-parse HEAD` equals `git rev-parse origin/main`
4. Report the commit SHA and GitHub commits URL to the user
5. Do not conflate "git push" with "deployed to production" - deployment is separate

## Common False Alarm

| Symptom | Actual cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| "ahead by N commits" after push | Stale remote-tracking ref or wrong upstream | `git fetch origin && git branch -u origin/main main` |
| Two remotes, same URL | Duplicate remote added (e.g. maya-space + origin) | Remove duplicate: `git remote remove <name>` |
| GitHub UI looks unchanged | Browser cache or viewing wrong branch | Hard refresh; confirm `main` at github.com/xiu-shi/maya_v1.0 |

## Model-Agnostic

Push and tracking behaviour is git configuration, not model-specific. Any agent must follow this rule regardless of which model is active.
